        "Subsection 4.4.21 — Exploring Counterfactual Moves Live Without Touching the Bus. The cutaway instrument below connects directly to Mission Readiness's `dominumIndex` alongside the `dominumLift` minimum-step solver (`academyInstruments.tsx`), allowing full counterfactual experimentation in read-only isolation from the live MissionEngine bus. Its five built-in presets reproduce the canonical benchmarks proved in Section III: \"Base case\" (`76.0`, Self-Reinforcing Dominium), \"Escrow frozen\" (`56.0`, Fiduciary Anchor), \"Floor breached\" (`79.8`, Custodial Inversion), \"Imperium-bound\" (`25.0`, Imperium-Bound), and \"Drill Beta final\" (`68.7`, Custodial Inversion). Each bar above the sliders scales visually against its ceiling share (30, 25, 25, and 20), letting you compare lost headroom across all four terms in a single glance while the threshold bar marks 40, 60, and 75.",
        "Run four structured experiments inside the instrument before attempting the comprehension check. First, select \"Base case\" (`76.0`) and press the Frozen toggle: verify that the fiduciary bar collapses instantaneously from 20.0 to zero, shifting the total marker twenty points left of 60 into Fiduciary Anchor, and confirm that `dominumLift` identifies lifting the freeze (`1 step`) as the lone rapid rescue lever. Also record how `Working` substitutes all four three-decimal normalised terms directly beneath the formula block, proving numerical fidelity to Desk 15. Second, select \"Floor breached\" (`79.8`): note that the index bar stands nearly five points beyond the 75 mark yet the verdict warns that the Communal bond sits at 3.0, while the solver grid proves that raising the Communal bond to 3.1 (`1 step`) is the sole decisive move whereas escrow (already 80, capped at 100), survival, and rupture cannot unlock the top phase regardless of slider position.",
