        "Subsection 4.4.22 — Primary Reading List and Codex Cross-References. For doctoral and practitioner study accompanying this chapter: (1) Justinian's Digest (Book 1, Title 21 and Book 41, Title 1–2; Ulpian's fragments distinguishing jurisdictional magistracy *imperium* from custodial title *dominium*), read alongside Francisco de Vitoria, *De Indis* (1532) on political jurisdiction vs. indigenous title and Hugo Grotius, *De Jure Belli ac Pacis* (1625, Book II, Chapter 3) on territorial jurisdiction versus property stewardship; (2) Martti Koskenniemi, *To the Uttermost Parts of the Earth: Legal Imagination and International Power, 1300–1870* (Cambridge University Press, 2021), especially Chapters 1–4 tracing how European legal doctrine braided *imperium* and *dominium* into sovereign governance; (3) Memorandum of Understanding between the Government of the Republic of Indonesia and the Free Aceh Movement, Helsinki, 15 August 2005, EU Council Joint Action 2005/643/CFSP establishing the Aceh Monitoring Mission, and Republic of Indonesia Law No. 11 of 2006 on the Governing of Aceh (particularly resource-sharing and Special Autonomy Fund Articles 179–184); (4) Belfast (Good Friday) Agreement of 10 April 1998, Independent International Commission on Decommissioning (IICD) Final Report (September 2005 / July 2011), and the St Andrews Agreement (October 2006); (5) OECD and European Commission Joint Research Centre, *Handbook on Constructing Composite Indicators: Methodology and User Guide* (OECD Publishing, 2008), Chapter 5 comparing linear, geometric, and non-compensatory multi-criteria aggregation; and (6) *The Vinculum Codex and Compact*, Appendix I (*The Dominum Effect*), Part XIV (Analyst Synthesis & Mission Readiness), Handbook Section 12D (Mandate Handover), and Appendix B (Reconciliation Register).",
