            "Sensitivity analysis is therefore not an optional flourish. A robust briefing can show whether a small plausible change in an input moves the result across a phase boundary, whether the reading is being carried by one component, and whether a classification depends on a bond that is close to the floor. The engine and the existing proof functions remain the authority for the official figure. An analyst may use a separate sensitivity calculation to understand uncertainty, but must label it as such and must never publish it as an alternative engine output.",
            "For applied research, this chapter can be read alongside work on measurement validity, causal inference, and peacebuilding evaluation. The key methodological lesson is that an index can summarise the state of specified conditions but cannot establish that the conditions caused a political outcome. A historical settlement that survived after the score would have been high does not validate the formula; a settlement that collapsed after a favourable reading does not, by itself, disprove every component. Evaluation requires an independent research design and evidence beyond the index."
