        {
          title: "Interpreting changes without mistaking arithmetic for political movement",
          paragraphs: [
            "The same total can arise from different combinations of its inputs. One state may have stronger bonds and weaker succession durability; another may have the reverse. The weighted sum can coincide while the practical risks differ. This is a general property of many-to-one mappings: aggregation is useful for compression, but information is necessarily lost when a vector is represented by one scalar.",
            "Accordingly, a change in the aggregate should be decomposed before it is narrated. If the total rises, identify which component changed and whether its change came from a new observation, an updated rule application, or a correction of the record. If the total remains steady, do not assume nothing happened; offsetting movements may have occurred. The displayed contributions and upstream evidence are the proper place to examine that possibility.",
            "The phase classifier introduces a further discontinuity. A continuous change in one component may produce no visible phase change until a boundary is crossed, after which a small additional increment changes the label. This does not mean that the political world itself changed discontinuously at that exact point. It means the classification rule partitions a continuous range into named intervals. The analyst should report the numeric movement as well as the categorical movement.",
            "Institutional transition also involves mandates that an index cannot confer. The United Nations Peacebuilding Commission describes itself as an intergovernmental advisory body supporting peace efforts in conflict-affected countries. That role is materially different from an operational authority to certify a mission's readiness, direct a drawdown, or impose obligations on parties. The Dominum result can be included as one documented input to a review, but the competent political and legal authorities retain responsibility for the decision and must consider mandate, consent, protection risks, and the applicable agreements. A high score is not a delegation of authority; a low score is not, by itself, a legal ground to prolong or terminate an operation.",
            "The Commission's mandate illustrates the positive work that can still follow from an advisory role: it brings relevant actors together, advises on integrated post-conflict recovery strategies, supports attention to institution-building and predictable financing, and provides a bridge among United Nations organs and other participants. The General Assembly and Security Council also describe its political accompaniment as being provided with the affected country's consent. These functions can inform how a transition review is organized, but they do not turn the Commission into a technical certifier of local capacity. The index must not borrow institutional authority from the body whose work it merely summarizes.",
            "This distinction is relevant to how transitions are documented. A defensible review should identify which body made the decision, the authority under which it acted, what evidence it considered, and how affected national and local institutions participated. The index records only four bus readings and its own phase rule; it does not record consultation quality, the distribution of transition costs, or whether the proposed handover has the necessary public legitimacy. Those matters may be discussed alongside it, but should not be silently treated as if they were measured by its output.",
            "The strict floor rule makes this point particularly clear. A bond just below and a bond just above the floor may be substantively similar in field conditions, yet the phase treatment differs because the rule is binary. The correct response is not to soften the comparison, but to explain both the mathematical condition and the uncertainty in the measurement that locates the bond near it.",
            "A time series should retain precision sufficient to reproduce the engine's classifications, while public prose can translate the result into readable language. If values are rounded for a chart, retain the underlying values in the auditable record and do not round in a way that changes whether a strict condition holds. Documentation should specify the display precision separately from the value used by the calculation."
          ]
        },
        {
          title: "A seminar exercise in model criticism and responsible use",
          paragraphs: [
            "Ask students to take the existing base case and write a short account of what it does establish. The account should describe the four inputs, the weighted aggregation, the phase logic, and the bond-floor check. It should then list at least three claims that the index cannot establish, such as popular consent, the absence of coercion, or the causal effect of an intervention. This exercise rewards precision rather than confidence.",
            "A second task is to compare two possible reports of the same state: one that gives only the total and phase, and one that includes component headroom, floor status, observation provenance, and a limitation statement. Students should explain how the second report changes what a decision-maker can verify. The point is not to make every public brief long, but to identify the minimum context needed to avoid a misleading interpretation.",
            "A third task is to use the published cutaway to alter a single input and record the result. The student should not invent an alternative formula or change any constant. They should distinguish the numerical effect of the change from the phase effect, and describe whether the change is supported by evidence or merely proposed as a scenario. The exercise makes counterfactual reasoning concrete while preserving the engine as the single source of truth.",
            "For a more advanced paper, students can compare the index's linear aggregation and viability gate with a different method discussed in the OECD-JRC handbook. The comparison should be methodological, not an attempted replacement of the official desk. It should ask which assumptions each aggregation encodes, how missing data are handled, whether the result is sensitive to weights, and what information is lost. A well-argued critique can recognize a design choice without claiming that all alternatives are equivalent.",
            "The final task is a source audit. For each historical statement, students identify whether it comes from a signed text, an official institutional history, a contemporary report, or a scholarly interpretation. They should mark any sentence that attributes causation or legal effect and verify that the source can support that claim. This is especially important when comparing a normative curriculum doctrine with treaties and domestic laws.",
            "The seminar's central lesson is that rigorous use requires both computational fidelity and epistemic restraint. The formula should be reproduced exactly; the prose should state what the formula means and what it leaves undecided. Neither requirement is a concession to the other. Together they make the synthesis more useful to scholars, practitioners, and the communities whose conditions are being described."
          ]
        },
        {
          title: "The decision record as a bridge between measurement and accountability",
          paragraphs: [
            "The Mission Readiness page is most useful when its result can be carried into an accountable decision record. That record should preserve the date, the component readings, the phase logic, and the condition of the weakest bond, then connect them to the action actually considered. A later reviewer can then determine whether the decision followed from the evidence available at the time or whether it relied on facts learned afterward.",
            "The record should also make disagreement legible. If one party disputes the quality of a verification process or the fairness of a fiscal arrangement, that objection should not be erased by reporting a single combined score. It may affect whether a component is well supported, whether the instrument is legitimate, or whether the proposed response is appropriate. The number can organize the discussion without deciding who is right.",
            "For institutional transitions, accountability includes the distribution of authority after departure. Identify which office will perform each function, who can review its decisions, what remedy is available when it fails, and whether affected people can reach that remedy in practice. These are familiar questions in public administration and rule-of-law analysis, but they are not all encoded in the four-term synthesis.",
            "A phased drawdown can therefore be designed as a learning process rather than a pass-fail ceremony. Each step can be paired with continued observation, scheduled review, and a route to correct a weakness. The Academy's phase labels provide a common vocabulary for one portion of that review; the mandate and the applicable legal instruments continue to govern authority and obligations.",
            "The final discipline is to avoid converting a framework into a promise. No calculated state can guarantee that an institution will remain effective, that political incentives will remain stable, or that future shocks will be absorbed. What the calculation offers is a transparent present-tense statement of selected conditions, suitable for scrutiny, challenge, and revision as new evidence arrives."
          ]
        },
        {
          title: "Concluding synthesis",
          paragraphs: [
            "The Dominum Index should be read as a compact, reproducible view of four published readings, governed by a separately stated phase rule and a strict viability condition. Its value lies in making the arithmetic inspectable and the gaps discussable. Its limit is equally important: a score cannot confer legal authority, settle political legitimacy, or guarantee a durable transfer of custody. Keep those propositions together whenever the index enters a scholarly argument or an operational brief."
          ]
        },
        {
          title: "A final rule of interpretation",
          paragraphs: [
            "Treat the classification as a statement about the model's present inputs, not about the future. Preserve the underlying record, give parties a way to challenge inaccurate evidence, and keep the mandate and applicable law in view when translating a reading into action. If the number and the qualitative record appear to diverge, investigate the divergence rather than allowing either one to erase the other. In that disciplined role, the synthesis can assist accountable judgment while remaining subordinate to the institutions and rights that give a transition its real-world meaning."
          ]
        },
        {
          title: "Closing note on the limits of synthesis",
          paragraphs: [
            "The number is a shared point of reference, not a verdict on a people or a settlement's moral worth. Its practical value depends on transparent inputs, a faithful calculation, meaningful avenues to contest the record, and a decision-maker who remains answerable for the action taken. Used on those terms, it can clarify discussion; detached from them, even a correct calculation can become an instrument of false certainty."
          ]
        },
        {
          title: "Carrying the reading forward",
          paragraphs: [
            "Preserve the complete input state with every handover, including its provenance and the phase condition that controlled classification. The next reader should be able to reproduce the result, challenge an inaccurate input, and understand which legal authority governs any proposed action. That continuity is the practical test of whether a synthesis is serving accountable institutional custody rather than merely producing a persuasive display."
          ]
        }
